    Add Position Rank column; fix PPG to use nflverse games-played
    
    Position Rank: "<rank by Total Points> (<rank by PPG>)" among
    same-position players for that season, 1 = best, shown on each player
    card's Fantasy Stats by Year table. Computed from the player's
    combined full-season total (not a partial-stint total), so a player
    traded mid-season shows the same rank on both of that season's rows.
    
    Also folds in the PPG fix: Sleeper's weekly matchup data has no
    reliable "did not play" signal -- a bye week or an injury-missed game
    still shows up as 0 points for a rostered player, same as a
    played-but-scoreless game. fetch_nflverse_played_weeks() now
    cross-references each player's Sleeper ID against nflverse's official
    box-score stats (via nflreadr::load_ff_playerids() + load_player_stats(),
    both already project dependencies through ffscrapr/ffsimulator) to
    count true games played instead. Total Points is unchanged -- still
    summed from Sleeper's own league-scored weekly totals. Players
    nflverse doesn't track individually (team DEF, or any unmapped ID)
    fall back to the previous nonzero-points heuristic.
    
